1
00:00:07,625 --> 00:00:09,025
SAY NO TO PIRACY, SUPPORT ORIGINALS

2
00:02:03,945 --> 00:02:05,505
After that day,

3
00:02:06,025 --> 00:02:08,665
it feels like Luan Nian
has put a spell on me.

4
00:02:09,425 --> 00:02:11,625
He unlocked the secret of my desire.

5
00:02:15,505 --> 00:02:16,825
Did you notice?

6
00:02:17,505 --> 00:02:18,785
You cannot control the feelings of love.

7
00:02:20,185 --> 00:02:22,425
And all those years,
he made me long for more.

8
00:02:22,505 --> 00:02:24,065
He drove me crazy and lived in my mind.

9
00:02:24,985 --> 00:02:27,425
Shang Zhitao, are you sober?

10
00:02:28,625 --> 00:02:30,585
Do you understand
what's going to happen next?

11
00:02:30,665 --> 00:02:32,985
I spent six years

12
00:02:33,585 --> 00:02:36,265
in this shameful, hidden relationship.

13
00:02:37,225 --> 00:02:39,705
There were grievances, pain,

14
00:02:40,785 --> 00:02:42,585
and joy.

15
00:02:43,825 --> 00:02:48,385
Yet I can never
take the first step to leave him.

16
00:02:51,225 --> 00:02:55,825
ADAPTED FROM THE EARLY SPRING ON JJWXC.NET
AUTHOR: GU NIANG BIE KU

17
00:02:58,225 --> 00:03:01,705
"YOU ARE NOT SUITABLE"

18
00:04:17,184 --> 00:04:18,785
The interview is about to begin, Luke.

19
00:04:19,745 --> 00:04:21,425
Shang Zhitao.

20
00:04:22,225 --> 00:04:25,025
Hi. I am Liang Xin, Lime's HR manager.

21
00:04:25,105 --> 00:04:26,505
You can call me Tracy.

22
00:04:27,105 --> 00:04:29,185
Today, your chief interviewer
is Luke Luan.

23
00:04:29,785 --> 00:04:32,305
If you're ready, let's begin.

24
00:04:33,185 --> 00:04:34,225
Okay.

25
00:04:35,545 --> 00:04:36,825
I am Shang Zhitao.

26
00:04:36,905 --> 00:04:38,225
My English name is Flora.

27
00:04:38,305 --> 00:04:41,225
I am from Harbin,
and I attended university in Nanjing.

28
00:04:41,305 --> 00:04:42,545
I'm a fresh graduate.

29
00:04:42,625 --> 00:04:45,025
I would love to work at Lime.

30
00:04:45,105 --> 00:04:47,065
Tell me about your work experience.

31
00:04:48,825 --> 00:04:50,505
MUTE, HANG UP, CAMERA

32
00:04:52,105 --> 00:04:53,225
Have you done any internships?

33
00:04:53,305 --> 00:04:54,945
If you have, tell us about that.

34
00:04:55,025 --> 00:04:56,145
I have.

35
00:04:56,225 --> 00:04:57,745
While I was in college,

36
00:04:57,825 --> 00:05:00,705
I did some scenic area planning projects
with my classmates.

37
00:05:00,785 --> 00:05:03,665
We planned the event's itinerary,

38
00:05:03,745 --> 00:05:06,905
set up the stage, and worked on posters
and promotional texts.

39
00:05:06,985 --> 00:05:08,185
How big was the project?

40
00:05:08,705 --> 00:05:10,545
There wasn't much funding,

41
00:05:10,625 --> 00:05:12,425
but we were very interested in it,

42
00:05:12,505 --> 00:05:15,265
so we joined with the goal
of gaining experience in mind--

43
00:05:15,345 --> 00:05:16,265
Okay.

44
00:05:16,865 --> 00:05:17,905
Next.

45
00:05:25,305 --> 00:05:27,265
Thank you, Shang Zhitao.

46
00:05:27,345 --> 00:05:29,625
That's all for your interview.

47
00:05:29,705 --> 00:05:31,025
Please go back and wait for our notice.

48
00:05:31,105 --> 00:05:34,665
It wasn't a huge project,
but I gained a lot of experience.

49
00:05:34,745 --> 00:05:36,265
Maybe I can share it with you?

50
00:05:36,345 --> 00:05:39,345
No need. I need someone
with top-tier hands-on experience.

51
00:05:39,425 --> 00:05:41,505
You're not suitable. Next.

52
00:05:46,985 --> 00:05:48,025
Thank you.

53
00:05:58,985 --> 00:06:00,105
Luke.

54
00:06:00,185 --> 00:06:03,585
Is it possible for you to mind
your tone during interviews?

55
00:06:03,665 --> 00:06:05,505
Let them finish speaking, at least.

56
00:06:07,065 --> 00:06:08,145
Sure.

57
00:06:16,265 --> 00:06:17,425
Yao Bei.

58
00:06:17,505 --> 00:06:19,145
I failed the interview.

59
00:06:20,425 --> 00:06:21,425
What happened?

60
00:06:21,945 --> 00:06:24,305
Tao. I have to work overtime today.

61
00:06:24,385 --> 00:06:25,985
Let's meet up and talk another day, okay?

62
00:06:26,505 --> 00:06:30,665
It's okay. I just arrived downstairs
at the flat I'm renting.

63
00:06:30,745 --> 00:06:33,465
Once I find my unit, I'll settle in.

64
00:06:33,985 --> 00:06:36,745
Okay. Take your time planning.
Don't give up.

65
00:06:36,825 --> 00:06:39,865
It's normal to be rejected
by a renowned company like Lime.

66
00:06:39,945 --> 00:06:41,585
Getting in is like winning the lottery.

67
00:06:42,305 --> 00:06:43,425
I know.

68
00:06:43,505 --> 00:06:44,505
All right then.

69
00:06:54,105 --> 00:06:55,785
TIANTONG DONGYUAN, SECTION 1

70
00:07:32,305 --> 00:07:33,225
Looking for someone?

71
00:07:34,145 --> 00:07:35,425
Sorry to bother you.

72
00:07:35,505 --> 00:07:37,545
I'm the new tenant.

73
00:07:37,625 --> 00:07:38,625
I contacted Zhang Lei.

74
00:07:41,745 --> 00:07:42,985
He's the landlord.

75
00:07:43,545 --> 00:07:44,625
Come in.

76
00:07:49,745 --> 00:07:50,825
Your room is here.

77
00:08:11,985 --> 00:08:15,465
It wasn't a huge project,
but I gained a lot of experience.

78
00:08:15,545 --> 00:08:17,905
-Maybe I can share them with you?
-No need.

79
00:08:17,985 --> 00:08:20,185
You're not suitable. Next.

80
00:08:24,945 --> 00:08:26,465
He didn't even let me finish.

81
00:08:28,865 --> 00:08:29,865
It's okay.

82
00:08:30,785 --> 00:08:33,545
Man proposes, God disposes.

83
00:08:42,945 --> 00:08:44,985
Tao. Have you arrived in Beijing?

84
00:08:45,065 --> 00:08:46,265
Have you settled in?

85
00:08:46,345 --> 00:08:48,385
How are your unit and your housemate?

86
00:08:52,505 --> 00:08:54,225
I've arrived. Everything is good.

87
00:08:54,305 --> 00:08:55,505
Don't worry.

88
00:09:03,145 --> 00:09:04,105
FOLLOW-UP E-MAIL TO LIME ADVERTISING
REGARDING MY WORK EXPERIENCE

89
00:09:04,185 --> 00:09:05,185
I AM AN ADVERTISING STUDENT AT JINLING
UNIVERSITY OF FINANCE AND ECONOMICS

90
00:09:05,265 --> 00:09:06,185
I'VE FOLLOWED LIME'S OUTSTANDING WORK
IN BRANDING AND CREATIVE PLANNING

91
00:09:06,265 --> 00:09:08,025
A habitual thief, aren't you?

92
00:09:08,105 --> 00:09:09,945
You keep stealing
my detergent and shampoo.

93
00:09:10,025 --> 00:09:11,145
Don't you dare make things up.

94
00:09:11,225 --> 00:09:12,665
I could say you stole my rings
and earrings.

95
00:09:12,745 --> 00:09:13,905
Liar!

96
00:09:13,985 --> 00:09:16,105
My bracelet was on the sink counter.

97
00:09:16,185 --> 00:09:17,465
When I came back ten minutes later,
it was gone.

98
00:09:17,545 --> 00:09:19,545
Only you went to the toilet.
So you must be the thief.

99
00:09:19,625 --> 00:09:20,545
I did not steal it.

100
00:09:20,625 --> 00:09:21,865
If you slander us again,
I'll tear your mouth off.

101
00:09:21,945 --> 00:09:24,105
You lost something?
Maybe we should call the police.

102
00:09:25,105 --> 00:09:26,905
Who are you? Why are you in my house?

103
00:09:26,985 --> 00:09:28,105
Right. Call the police.

104
00:09:28,185 --> 00:09:29,345
Now.

105
00:09:29,425 --> 00:09:30,745
Call the police. Where's your phone?

106
00:09:30,825 --> 00:09:32,185
What gives you the right
to say whatever you want?

107
00:09:32,265 --> 00:09:34,065
Look at how crazy you are.

108
00:09:34,145 --> 00:09:35,945
You always look miserable.
No wonder you're single.

109
00:09:36,025 --> 00:09:37,945
Your man lies in bed all day.
He doesn't go to work.

110
00:09:38,025 --> 00:09:39,145
"Honey, wash my socks."

111
00:09:39,225 --> 00:09:40,945
"Honey, wash my underwear."
"Wash it for me."

112
00:09:41,025 --> 00:09:42,785
Is it fun washing someone's
dirty underwear?

113
00:09:42,865 --> 00:09:45,505
-I do what I want.
-Don't fight.

114
00:09:45,585 --> 00:09:46,985
-Don't hit her.
-Move!

115
00:09:50,905 --> 00:09:51,745
Let her go!

116
00:09:51,825 --> 00:09:52,785
Come.

117
00:09:54,585 --> 00:09:55,945
Lock the door.

118
00:09:56,025 --> 00:09:57,385
-Open the door!
-Open the door!

119
00:09:57,465 --> 00:09:58,305
You hit me. I'll call the police.

120
00:10:02,785 --> 00:10:04,345
-Open the door!
-Hello, 110?

121
00:10:04,425 --> 00:10:05,385
I want to make a report.

122
00:10:18,305 --> 00:10:19,345
Come in.

123
00:10:23,545 --> 00:10:25,625
The shortlist
for this graduate recruitment.

124
00:10:25,705 --> 00:10:26,585
Please sign it.

125
00:10:28,905 --> 00:10:31,105
GRADUATE RECRUITMENT SHORTLISTED
CANDIDATES, 5. SHANG ZHITAO

126
00:10:33,585 --> 00:10:34,665
Shang Zhitao?

127
00:10:36,185 --> 00:10:38,865
I thought I rejected her
during the interview.

128
00:10:39,465 --> 00:10:42,225
Yes. You did.

129
00:10:42,305 --> 00:10:43,465
But Luke,

130
00:10:43,545 --> 00:10:46,345
HR is all about diverse employment.

131
00:10:46,425 --> 00:10:48,905
I wasn't born to be an HRBP.

132
00:10:48,985 --> 00:10:50,985
We all went through a learning process.

133
00:10:51,625 --> 00:10:54,305
Our company has fielded
many competent individuals,

134
00:10:54,385 --> 00:10:57,025
but they're all too high up
and out of touch with reality.

135
00:10:57,665 --> 00:11:01,065
If this continues,
the team will have problems.

136
00:11:01,905 --> 00:11:04,385
But we can't recruit someone with
neither qualifications nor experience.

137
00:11:05,305 --> 00:11:06,505
Is she a relative of yours?

138
00:11:07,705 --> 00:11:09,745
Are you doubting my professionalism?

139
00:11:09,825 --> 00:11:11,585
You didn't even let her finish.

140
00:11:11,665 --> 00:11:13,425
After the interview,
she proactively sent me

141
00:11:13,505 --> 00:11:15,225
supplementary materials about her project.

142
00:11:15,305 --> 00:11:17,185
Her feedback in the background check
was the best.

143
00:11:17,265 --> 00:11:18,945
I have discussed this with headquarters.

144
00:11:19,025 --> 00:11:22,665
This time, I'll recruit
some down-to-earth fresh graduates.

145
00:11:23,185 --> 00:11:24,665
Consider this an experiment of mine.

146
00:11:25,265 --> 00:11:28,145
Besides, your Lumi
keeps asking me for more manpower.

147
00:11:28,225 --> 00:11:32,505
Can you please support my endeavor
and sign on the paper?

148
00:11:34,665 --> 00:11:35,825
Fine. This is a favor.

149
00:11:36,465 --> 00:11:38,225
Sure. I owe you one.

150
00:11:39,025 --> 00:11:41,065
The new recruits will report next Monday.

151
00:11:41,145 --> 00:11:42,865
Find some time and meet with them.

152
00:11:42,945 --> 00:11:44,905
You were at the training seminar
last year, right?

153
00:11:46,025 --> 00:11:48,825
I wasn't able to answer those questions.

154
00:11:49,425 --> 00:11:51,585
"Is office romance allowed?"

155
00:11:51,665 --> 00:11:55,625
Tracy, you're the one who decides
who gets to join our company.

156
00:11:55,705 --> 00:11:57,105
Please use your power wisely.

157
00:11:57,785 --> 00:11:58,825
Okay.

158
00:11:58,905 --> 00:12:00,185
I shall return and add

159
00:12:00,265 --> 00:12:02,145
"No asking about
your superior's personal life"

160
00:12:02,225 --> 00:12:05,465
and "No dating
between superiors and subordinates"

161
00:12:05,545 --> 00:12:08,865
to the new recruit's manual
in black and white. Happy?

162
00:12:08,945 --> 00:12:10,825
Congratulations. You've become
more and more professional.

163
00:12:12,065 --> 00:12:13,385
I shall go now.

164
00:12:20,265 --> 00:12:21,665
FARMHOUSE PORK

165
00:12:23,785 --> 00:12:26,425
So, you won't file
a police report anymore?

166
00:12:28,145 --> 00:12:29,865
I've checked with Lei.

167
00:12:29,945 --> 00:12:33,105
He said they had already mentioned
moving out last month.

168
00:12:33,185 --> 00:12:37,545
Why else would they pack up so quickly
and leave while we were hiding?

169
00:12:39,385 --> 00:12:40,585
She stole my things. So be it.

170
00:12:40,665 --> 00:12:42,625
She can have them. I don't need them.

171
00:12:42,705 --> 00:12:43,665
Thank you for today.

172
00:12:43,745 --> 00:12:45,665
I am Sun Yu. What's your name?

173
00:12:46,345 --> 00:12:47,745
I am Shang Zhitao.

174
00:12:47,825 --> 00:12:49,385
Shang Zhitao.

175
00:12:52,145 --> 00:12:53,105
Thank you.

176
00:12:54,465 --> 00:12:57,705
I've never asked you this.
What do you do for work?

177
00:12:59,065 --> 00:12:59,945
Love business.

178
00:13:02,305 --> 00:13:06,865
I work in sales for a dating site.

179
00:13:06,945 --> 00:13:08,585
Isn't that love business?

180
00:13:11,825 --> 00:13:12,865
Where are you from?

181
00:13:13,465 --> 00:13:15,505
Me? I'm from Harbin.

182
00:13:15,585 --> 00:13:17,745
But I went to university in Nanjing.

183
00:13:19,465 --> 00:13:20,465
Nanjing?

184
00:13:22,785 --> 00:13:23,905
My ex is from Nanjing.

185
00:13:25,905 --> 00:13:27,945
I… Sorry.

186
00:13:28,025 --> 00:13:29,345
Don't be.

187
00:13:29,425 --> 00:13:31,105
He should be the one apologizing to me.

188
00:13:31,705 --> 00:13:34,505
He kept saying the feelings had faded.

189
00:13:35,025 --> 00:13:37,225
But I know he thinks
I'm not good enough for him.

190
00:13:38,305 --> 00:13:39,665
In Beijing,

191
00:13:40,505 --> 00:13:43,265
everyone has a price.

192
00:13:45,025 --> 00:13:46,625
They are waiting for the best offer.

193
00:13:48,745 --> 00:13:50,625
You're too good for him.

194
00:13:50,705 --> 00:13:51,745
He will surely regret it.

195
00:13:52,625 --> 00:13:53,985
Impossible.

196
00:13:55,505 --> 00:13:57,145
I won't let him hurt me again.

197
00:13:57,865 --> 00:13:59,025
You're right.

198
00:13:59,105 --> 00:14:01,105
Don't let anyone hurt you again.

199
00:14:01,185 --> 00:14:02,225
Exactly.

200
00:14:03,385 --> 00:14:04,585
Screw love.

201
00:14:06,185 --> 00:14:07,665
I will be rich.

202
00:14:09,105 --> 00:14:12,505
I won't let stupid romance weigh me down.

203
00:14:14,105 --> 00:14:14,945
You have my support.

204
00:14:15,025 --> 00:14:16,665
I agree with you.

205
00:14:16,745 --> 00:14:20,505
When we're self-sufficient,
love will come after us.

206
00:14:21,305 --> 00:14:22,345
Good one.

207
00:14:23,745 --> 00:14:26,105
Meeting you is the beginning
of my good fortune. Thank you.

208
00:14:27,665 --> 00:14:28,505
Actually, I'm the lucky one.

209
00:14:28,585 --> 00:14:30,465
It's my first day in Beijing,
and someone is buying me a meal.

210
00:14:30,545 --> 00:14:32,345
You're so kind and brave.

211
00:14:32,905 --> 00:14:35,505
People will queue up to buy you a meal.

212
00:14:36,025 --> 00:14:37,785
Dig in. You haven't touched anything.

213
00:14:55,785 --> 00:14:59,025
OFFER LETTER
BEIJING LIME ADVERTISING

214
00:15:04,065 --> 00:15:07,505
OFFER LETTER
DEAR SHANG ZHITAO…

215
00:15:14,825 --> 00:15:17,705
Tao, can I come in?

216
00:15:20,185 --> 00:15:22,225
Thank you for today.

217
00:15:25,585 --> 00:15:27,025
What's the matter?

218
00:15:27,105 --> 00:15:28,185
Why are you crying?

219
00:15:30,225 --> 00:15:31,345
What happened?

220
00:15:33,105 --> 00:15:35,665
I… I found a job.

221
00:15:35,745 --> 00:15:37,465
You… You found a job?

222
00:15:38,065 --> 00:15:40,225
-Where?
-Lime.

223
00:15:41,465 --> 00:15:42,665
Lime?

224
00:15:42,745 --> 00:15:43,705
Seriously?

225
00:15:43,785 --> 00:15:46,705
The Lime that made
the Olympic advertisements?

226
00:15:47,425 --> 00:15:49,665
Is this for real, Shang Zhitao?

227
00:15:52,385 --> 00:15:53,745
Beijing Lime.

228
00:15:54,385 --> 00:15:56,545
You're amazing!

229
00:15:59,425 --> 00:16:01,345
I was about to give this to you.

230
00:16:01,945 --> 00:16:03,585
You told me you were looking for a job.

231
00:16:03,665 --> 00:16:04,985
I got this lucky charm from Yonghe Temple.

232
00:16:05,065 --> 00:16:06,385
It will boost your career.

233
00:16:09,585 --> 00:16:11,065
Thank you, Sun Yu.

234
00:16:11,145 --> 00:16:14,225
-I really need it.
-You are so amazing.

235
00:17:03,505 --> 00:17:04,665
Luke.

236
00:17:04,745 --> 00:17:05,905
I need to tell you something.

237
00:17:06,745 --> 00:17:07,825
An emergency?

238
00:17:07,905 --> 00:17:09,665
Qipai is very happy
with the annual plan we proposed.

239
00:17:10,865 --> 00:17:12,704
-So we sign now.
-No.

240
00:17:12,785 --> 00:17:13,865
Something bad happened.

241
00:17:16,665 --> 00:17:19,585
They plan to use our design proposal
for their secondary line brand.

242
00:17:19,665 --> 00:17:22,184
And they want a discount. 30% discount.

243
00:17:22,265 --> 00:17:23,184
No.

244
00:17:24,345 --> 00:17:26,265
Their Asia Pacific regional manager said

245
00:17:26,345 --> 00:17:28,985
that the secondary line brand
would be their main push this year.

246
00:17:29,065 --> 00:17:30,065
If our design proposal

247
00:17:30,145 --> 00:17:33,025
can help them boost this year's sales,

248
00:17:33,105 --> 00:17:35,425
next year, they'll let us
handle the marketing

249
00:17:35,505 --> 00:17:36,865
of all their brands under them.

250
00:17:36,945 --> 00:17:37,945
That's not good either.

251
00:17:40,065 --> 00:17:41,305
So we'll just lose the deal then.

252
00:17:42,025 --> 00:17:43,025
I'd rather lose them.

253
00:17:43,865 --> 00:17:46,625
They approved our proposal,
which means our ideas are good.

254
00:17:47,465 --> 00:17:50,025
They can choose to implement our proposals
on whichever product they want,

255
00:17:50,105 --> 00:17:51,385
but we won't give them a discount.

256
00:17:52,145 --> 00:17:54,265
Our ideas are not for hawking,

257
00:17:54,345 --> 00:17:56,065
where people expect us
to give them a huge discount.

258
00:17:56,745 --> 00:17:59,785
Okay. I'll confirm
the quotation with Finance.

259
00:18:02,745 --> 00:18:03,985
You look dashing today.

260
00:18:24,745 --> 00:18:26,105
Handle the file.

261
00:18:27,785 --> 00:18:29,505
-Morning, Luke.
-Morning, Luke.

262
00:18:31,905 --> 00:18:33,145
So, he is Luke.

263
00:18:37,785 --> 00:18:38,865
Morning, Luke.

264
00:18:43,585 --> 00:18:44,545
Morning.

265
00:18:56,865 --> 00:18:58,065
Luke.

266
00:18:59,025 --> 00:19:00,705
I'm the new recruit, Shang Zhitao.

267
00:19:00,785 --> 00:19:02,305
Thank you for recruiting me.

268
00:19:03,545 --> 00:19:05,785
No need to thank me.
I did not recruit you.

269
00:19:06,665 --> 00:19:08,585
In my eyes, you're not good enough.

270
00:19:11,705 --> 00:19:13,665
Then, I shall thank Lime
for this opportunity.

271
00:19:13,745 --> 00:19:14,865
I'll work hard.

272
00:19:17,065 --> 00:19:18,985
I hope you'll pass the probation,

273
00:19:19,545 --> 00:19:21,065
instead of just using us
to polish your resume before leaving.

274
00:19:26,305 --> 00:19:29,425
I am incredibly lucky and honored
to be able to work

275
00:19:29,505 --> 00:19:31,785
in this world-class advertising company.

276
00:19:31,865 --> 00:19:33,505
I will do my best to stay here.

277
00:19:38,225 --> 00:19:40,065
New hire? You know her?

278
00:19:41,865 --> 00:19:44,105
Why would I know a nobody
from the labor market?

279
00:19:47,745 --> 00:19:49,665
Who got him so upset
this early in the morning?

280
00:19:51,025 --> 00:19:52,345
We spoiled him, didn't we?

281
00:19:56,945 --> 00:19:58,065
Tracy.

282
00:20:05,105 --> 00:20:07,105
Welcome to Lime China.

283
00:20:07,185 --> 00:20:09,385
I am Liang Xin, the HR manager.

284
00:20:09,465 --> 00:20:11,865
In our company culture, we address
each other by our English names.

285
00:20:11,945 --> 00:20:13,305
So, please call me Tracy.

286
00:20:13,905 --> 00:20:17,625
Allow me to brief you and show you around.

287
00:20:18,305 --> 00:20:19,505
Come with me.

288
00:20:21,785 --> 00:20:24,905
What you're seeing now
is an introduction to our company.

289
00:20:25,705 --> 00:20:27,425
This is the Creative Division.

290
00:20:27,505 --> 00:20:28,625
Are you sure they want
to change it this way?

291
00:20:28,705 --> 00:20:30,305
It's the same as our first draft.

292
00:20:33,465 --> 00:20:34,305
START

293
00:20:34,385 --> 00:20:35,985
This is the Business Division.

294
00:20:36,065 --> 00:20:38,265
The busiest division in our company.

295
00:20:40,185 --> 00:20:42,625
I'll notify the supplier
about the client's request immediately

296
00:20:42,705 --> 00:20:44,025
so that they can find a new venue.

297
00:20:44,105 --> 00:20:44,825
The Commerce Division.

298
00:20:44,905 --> 00:20:45,825
We have a business negotiation
this afternoon.

299
00:20:45,905 --> 00:20:47,345
Get the collaboration proposal ready.

300
00:20:47,425 --> 00:20:48,145
Let's begin.

301
00:20:48,225 --> 00:20:49,425
This is the pantry.

302
00:20:49,505 --> 00:20:51,265
There's a lounge in the back.

303
00:20:51,785 --> 00:20:52,905
This is the public space.

304
00:20:52,985 --> 00:20:54,505
You can use it whenever you want.

305
00:20:54,585 --> 00:20:55,625
Recap of the situation. Last month…

306
00:20:55,705 --> 00:20:57,345
There are several restaurants
near the office.

307
00:20:57,425 --> 00:20:59,145
When you show your Lime work badge,
you'll get a 20% discount.

308
00:20:59,225 --> 00:21:02,025
You'll find the details
in the employee manual.

309
00:21:02,105 --> 00:21:03,825
Your probation period
will last for three months,

310
00:21:03,905 --> 00:21:05,345
and you'll rotate through divisions.

311
00:21:05,425 --> 00:21:07,865
Once you've decided to work
in a particular division,

312
00:21:07,945 --> 00:21:09,945
you may end the rotational shift.

313
00:21:10,025 --> 00:21:11,585
Have I made myself clear?

314
00:21:11,665 --> 00:21:12,585
Yes.

315
00:21:12,665 --> 00:21:15,545
Your first position
is in Business Division One.

316
00:21:15,625 --> 00:21:17,465
You will work under…

317
00:21:17,545 --> 00:21:18,465
Lumi.

318
00:21:18,545 --> 00:21:19,745
Tracy.

319
00:21:22,465 --> 00:21:23,345
Allow me to introduce.

320
00:21:24,065 --> 00:21:25,305
Lumi, your mentor.

321
00:21:25,385 --> 00:21:26,665
You'll be working for her.

322
00:21:27,465 --> 00:21:29,945
-Hi, madam.
-Wow.

323
00:21:30,025 --> 00:21:32,065
Are fresh graduates this nerdy nowadays?

324
00:21:32,145 --> 00:21:35,705
Perhaps you can show her
the true colors of corporate life.

325
00:21:35,785 --> 00:21:37,585
Please be nice to kids.

326
00:21:38,265 --> 00:21:39,425
Don't be like Luke.

327
00:21:40,145 --> 00:21:41,265
Tracy.

328
00:21:41,345 --> 00:21:44,505
Come on. I have no filter.

329
00:21:44,585 --> 00:21:47,225
But work is work.
Don't treat it like a joking matter.

330
00:21:47,305 --> 00:21:48,425
Worry not, madam.

331
00:21:48,505 --> 00:21:49,705
I'll work hard.

332
00:21:49,785 --> 00:21:50,945
All right.

333
00:21:51,025 --> 00:21:52,265
She'll work for me now.

334
00:21:52,345 --> 00:21:54,345
Come. Let me show you your desk.

335
00:21:55,105 --> 00:21:56,025
Don't worry.

336
00:21:57,985 --> 00:21:59,505
You'll sit here.

337
00:21:59,585 --> 00:22:00,905
Ms. Lumi.

338
00:22:00,985 --> 00:22:03,505
I am Shang Zhitao. Or Flora.

339
00:22:04,665 --> 00:22:06,465
No need to add "miss".

340
00:22:06,545 --> 00:22:08,265
Just call me Lumi.

341
00:22:08,345 --> 00:22:10,105
My English and Chinese names
are both Lumi.

342
00:22:11,945 --> 00:22:14,225
That row there
is the offices of all the bigwigs.

343
00:22:14,865 --> 00:22:18,225
And that one in particular, avoid it.

344
00:22:20,425 --> 00:22:21,745
Mr. Luan's office?

345
00:22:24,105 --> 00:22:25,185
You're smart.

346
00:22:25,825 --> 00:22:28,465
At work, just call him Luke.

347
00:22:28,545 --> 00:22:30,945
All right. I'll send you
some documents later.

348
00:22:31,025 --> 00:22:32,945
Familiarize yourself with our projects,

349
00:22:33,025 --> 00:22:34,665
and wait for my call.

350
00:22:35,545 --> 00:22:37,985
Oh. Report yourself to Luke first.

351
00:22:38,065 --> 00:22:41,625
While you do that,
conduct the interview as well.

352
00:22:41,705 --> 00:22:42,865
Compile your questions now.

353
00:22:42,945 --> 00:22:44,625
Interview?

354
00:22:44,705 --> 00:22:46,385
I will interview Luke?

355
00:22:46,465 --> 00:22:49,825
It is our tradition that the new hire
will interview the boss.

356
00:22:50,505 --> 00:22:52,345
Book an appointment with him today.

357
00:23:14,505 --> 00:23:15,745
Lumi.

358
00:23:16,345 --> 00:23:18,385
-You startled me.
-Sorry.

359
00:23:18,945 --> 00:23:23,625
I have a question.
Must I do the interview today?

360
00:23:26,345 --> 00:23:27,185
You're afraid of him?

361
00:23:28,945 --> 00:23:31,545
I heard he's quite strict.

362
00:23:31,625 --> 00:23:33,105
I'm just a bit worried.

363
00:23:35,665 --> 00:23:37,905
Creative people can be cranky.

364
00:23:37,985 --> 00:23:41,185
He's blunt, but he can be reasoned with.

365
00:23:41,265 --> 00:23:42,865
He won't devour you. Careful.

366
00:23:43,785 --> 00:23:45,985
He has already vented his anger today.

367
00:23:47,625 --> 00:23:49,865
He yelled at three people
until they cried at the morning meeting,

368
00:23:49,945 --> 00:23:51,545
so he probably won't yell again.

369
00:23:52,105 --> 00:23:55,505
What can I do to get along with him
if I don't want to be yelled at?

370
00:23:58,225 --> 00:23:59,665
Get along with him?

371
00:24:01,145 --> 00:24:02,145
Do you want to date him or something?

372
00:24:05,465 --> 00:24:06,905
You're blushing.

373
00:24:08,185 --> 00:24:09,025
I have one tip for you.

374
00:24:09,705 --> 00:24:12,545
At work, the more prideful your boss is,

375
00:24:12,625 --> 00:24:14,265
the more thick-skinned you have to be.

376
00:24:15,465 --> 00:24:16,505
Thick-skinned?

377
00:24:17,705 --> 00:24:18,905
Good luck.

378
00:24:46,305 --> 00:24:47,505
Come in.

379
00:24:55,105 --> 00:24:56,345
Hi, Luke.

380
00:24:56,425 --> 00:24:59,025
I am Shang Zhitao,
the new hire in Business Division One.

381
00:24:59,105 --> 00:25:00,145
You can call me Flora.

382
00:25:00,225 --> 00:25:01,745
Do you have time now?

383
00:25:01,825 --> 00:25:03,585
I have some questions for you.

384
00:25:04,425 --> 00:25:05,705
Is it urgent?

385
00:25:05,785 --> 00:25:07,225
Not really.

386
00:25:09,545 --> 00:25:10,625
Not urgent?

387
00:25:10,705 --> 00:25:11,625
Then, wait here.

388
00:25:43,745 --> 00:25:45,425
She doesn't hide a thing.

389
00:25:45,505 --> 00:25:48,025
You won't find
someone so guileless in Lime.

390
00:26:04,265 --> 00:26:05,705
Hello.

391
00:26:06,665 --> 00:26:07,825
Luan Nian.

392
00:26:07,905 --> 00:26:09,345
I don't want to break up.

393
00:26:09,425 --> 00:26:10,545
Can we…

394
00:26:10,625 --> 00:26:12,345
Can we sit down and talk things through?

395
00:26:12,425 --> 00:26:14,025
-Do not call me with a new number again.
-Luan Nian!

396
00:26:14,105 --> 00:26:15,065
‎Luan--

397
00:26:19,985 --> 00:26:21,065
Luke.

398
00:26:22,345 --> 00:26:23,185
Are you free now?

399
00:26:25,105 --> 00:26:25,985
You said it wasn't urgent.

400
00:26:27,585 --> 00:26:29,465
I assumed your time wasn't worth much,

401
00:26:29,545 --> 00:26:30,985
so your work could be deprioritized.

402
00:26:34,185 --> 00:26:35,345
I understand now.

403
00:26:35,425 --> 00:26:37,745
I will be direct about my needs
with you from now on.

404
00:26:37,825 --> 00:26:39,465
Thank you for the lesson.

405
00:26:39,545 --> 00:26:41,225
I did not teach you anything.
You may leave.

406
00:26:43,785 --> 00:26:46,345
Luke, according to the company's policy,

407
00:26:46,425 --> 00:26:48,585
you need to work with me as a new hire

408
00:26:48,665 --> 00:26:50,065
to have the interview.

409
00:26:50,145 --> 00:26:53,385
If you are not free today,
I'll follow up tomorrow.

410
00:26:53,465 --> 00:26:54,665
Just do it now.

411
00:26:57,025 --> 00:26:57,905
Sure.

412
00:27:00,985 --> 00:27:03,105
Why did you join Lime?

413
00:27:03,185 --> 00:27:04,145
The pay is great.

414
00:27:07,825 --> 00:27:08,665
The pay is great.

415
00:27:09,865 --> 00:27:13,145
-Do you like your job?
-No.

416
00:27:14,545 --> 00:27:17,025
Then, why are you staying?

417
00:27:19,145 --> 00:27:20,185
To make money and splurge.

418
00:27:23,385 --> 00:27:24,385
Okay.

419
00:27:24,985 --> 00:27:29,025
Allow me to share the projects I will be
joining in the future with you one by one.

420
00:27:29,105 --> 00:27:32,225
-I look forward to your further guidance.
-I will not guide you.

421
00:27:32,305 --> 00:27:33,345
You can just ask Lumi for anything.

422
00:27:34,265 --> 00:27:35,385
But I hope you can--

423
00:27:35,465 --> 00:27:37,425
Can you differentiate ROI and CVR?

424
00:27:37,505 --> 00:27:39,665
Can you use SWOT analysis
to market a product?

425
00:27:39,745 --> 00:27:42,625
Can you differentiate
between advertising channels?

426
00:27:43,945 --> 00:27:45,505
Sorry. Can you repeat?

427
00:27:45,585 --> 00:27:48,025
I'll take them down
and try to get back to you by tomorrow.

428
00:27:48,105 --> 00:27:50,025
If you really want a piece
of advice from me,

429
00:27:50,105 --> 00:27:52,145
it'll be to find a new job
as soon as possible.

430
00:27:52,665 --> 00:27:53,505
You're not fit for Lime.

431
00:28:01,465 --> 00:28:03,025
Why do you think

432
00:28:04,145 --> 00:28:05,145
I'm not a good fit?

433
00:28:11,265 --> 00:28:13,145
Academics-wise, you're average.

434
00:28:13,745 --> 00:28:15,825
Background-wise, you have no connections.

435
00:28:15,905 --> 00:28:18,745
Experience-wise, you have no experience
with large-scale advertising projects.

436
00:28:18,825 --> 00:28:20,305
What do you bring to the table?

437
00:28:20,905 --> 00:28:24,265
Why should I waste my time
on someone who will be replaced soon?

438
00:28:28,145 --> 00:28:29,465
I have been accepted into Lime.

439
00:28:29,545 --> 00:28:31,785
That means I must have some value.

440
00:28:32,425 --> 00:28:34,225
I will do my best to keep up with you.

441
00:28:34,305 --> 00:28:35,425
I won't waste your time.

442
00:28:35,505 --> 00:28:37,185
You're wasting everyone's time.

443
00:28:37,785 --> 00:28:39,105
You can't even understand what I'm saying.

444
00:28:39,185 --> 00:28:40,505
I don't deal with idiots.

445
00:28:42,065 --> 00:28:43,905
What kind of person do you like
to deal with then?

446
00:28:43,985 --> 00:28:45,985
-I can--
-I deal with jerks

447
00:28:46,065 --> 00:28:47,905
ike me. Can you do that?

448
00:28:53,305 --> 00:28:54,225
Okay.

449
00:28:55,185 --> 00:28:56,265
Duly noted.

450
00:28:56,345 --> 00:28:57,265
Thank you.

451
00:28:58,625 --> 00:28:59,505
I will go now.

452
00:29:10,985 --> 00:29:13,065
Sorry. I… I'll buy a new one.

453
00:29:15,785 --> 00:29:18,105
You can't afford it. Get out.

454
00:29:20,985 --> 00:29:22,185
Get out now.

455
00:29:35,345 --> 00:29:37,745
SHANG ZHITAO

456
00:29:44,465 --> 00:29:47,065
You must be the new intern.

457
00:29:48,105 --> 00:29:49,185
No, I'm not.

458
00:29:49,265 --> 00:29:51,505
I'm a full-time employee.

459
00:29:51,585 --> 00:29:53,345
Today is my first day.

460
00:29:53,425 --> 00:29:55,185
I am Shang Zhitao, Flora.

461
00:29:55,785 --> 00:29:56,745
Hi, I'm Jack.

462
00:29:57,425 --> 00:29:59,505
Are you free?
Can you get me a cup of coffee?

463
00:30:02,265 --> 00:30:03,185
Sure.

464
00:30:03,945 --> 00:30:04,945
Thank you.

465
00:30:05,025 --> 00:30:06,625
Does anyone else want coffee?

466
00:30:09,265 --> 00:30:10,225
You love making coffee that much?

467
00:30:11,425 --> 00:30:12,985
Why don't you make everyone
a cup of coffee?

468
00:30:13,705 --> 00:30:15,265
Lumi. Conference Room One.

469
00:30:15,345 --> 00:30:17,505
-Meeting in ten minutes.
-Noted.

470
00:30:18,345 --> 00:30:19,265
Iced Americano.

471
00:30:24,425 --> 00:30:28,185
Flora, from now on in this company,
ask me before you do anything.

472
00:30:28,265 --> 00:30:30,905
I am your mentor.
I'll tell you what to do.

473
00:30:30,985 --> 00:30:32,105
Do you hear me?

474
00:30:33,305 --> 00:30:34,745
-Yes.
-Don't be too meek.

475
00:30:34,825 --> 00:30:38,225
In this office,
people will bully the weak.

476
00:30:38,305 --> 00:30:40,145
The more sheepish you are,
the more they take advantage of you.

477
00:30:40,225 --> 00:30:41,745
They will then ask you to do
all the hard labor.

478
00:30:41,825 --> 00:30:42,665
You won't be able to take it.

479
00:30:44,985 --> 00:30:45,825
Have you conducted the interview?

480
00:30:47,145 --> 00:30:48,065
Yes.

481
00:30:48,865 --> 00:30:50,025
Lumi.

482
00:30:50,105 --> 00:30:53,785
Well, is the typewriter in Luke's office
very expensive?

483
00:30:53,865 --> 00:30:57,505
I ran into it just now,
and he said I could never afford it.

484
00:30:58,025 --> 00:30:59,265
You are quite something.

485
00:30:59,785 --> 00:31:00,985
He loves that thing.

486
00:31:01,065 --> 00:31:03,425
I'm not sure how expensive it is.

487
00:31:04,545 --> 00:31:05,985
Meeting first. We'll talk after.

488
00:31:19,105 --> 00:31:22,305
LEISURE WORK AREA

489
00:31:32,625 --> 00:31:33,745
MINUTES OF MANAGEMENT INTERVIEWS

490
00:31:33,825 --> 00:31:34,745
SEND

491
00:31:46,545 --> 00:31:48,105
Q&A OF THE INTERVIEW

492
00:31:48,185 --> 00:31:49,225
QUESTIONING OF PERSONAL CAPABILITIES
AND FUTURE PROJECTS

493
00:31:49,305 --> 00:31:50,025
THE LEADER REPEATEDLY USED NEGATIVE

494
00:31:50,105 --> 00:31:50,705
AND AGGRESSIVE LANGUAGE
DURING THE INTERVIEW

495
00:31:59,225 --> 00:32:00,065
Hello?

496
00:32:00,145 --> 00:32:03,265
You told the new hire
that you worked to splurge?

497
00:32:03,345 --> 00:32:04,185
TO MAKE MONEY AND SPLURGE

498
00:32:04,265 --> 00:32:05,785
Why are you staying
if you don't like the job?

499
00:32:05,865 --> 00:32:07,145
To make money and splurge.

500
00:32:08,745 --> 00:32:10,025
What else?

501
00:32:10,105 --> 00:32:11,305
And you told her to find a new job.

502
00:32:11,385 --> 00:32:12,665
I ADVISE YOU TO GET A NEW JOB

503
00:32:12,745 --> 00:32:13,905
You're not fit for Lime.

504
00:32:14,705 --> 00:32:15,705
Is that a problem?

505
00:32:15,785 --> 00:32:17,265
And you want her to be a jerk?

506
00:32:18,025 --> 00:32:19,385
What kind of person
do you like to deal with then?

507
00:32:19,465 --> 00:32:21,385
I deal with jerks.

508
00:32:21,985 --> 00:32:22,905
Is that a problem?

509
00:32:23,425 --> 00:32:26,265
The advertisement industry needs us
to be bold and yet unfazed by anything.

510
00:32:26,345 --> 00:32:28,665
Are you aware that your next promotion
is around the corner?

511
00:32:28,745 --> 00:32:31,625
Does that have anything to do
with the interview?

512
00:32:31,705 --> 00:32:33,385
Not directly,

513
00:32:33,465 --> 00:32:36,065
but you must respect
our diversity employment policy.

514
00:32:36,145 --> 00:32:37,505
I respect that,

515
00:32:37,585 --> 00:32:39,505
but it has nothing to do
with my opinion of her.

516
00:32:39,585 --> 00:32:40,785
What's so bad about her?

517
00:32:40,865 --> 00:32:43,145
It's her first day at work.

518
00:32:43,225 --> 00:32:44,865
If you weren't my junior,

519
00:32:44,945 --> 00:32:47,825
I would've reported you to the board
and asked them to fire you.

520
00:32:48,345 --> 00:32:49,545
Go ahead.

521
00:33:03,905 --> 00:33:05,305
She's indeed an idiot.

522
00:33:16,025 --> 00:33:19,465
JINGHUANANJIE STATION
OPERATION HOURS: 05:30-22:00

523
00:33:22,505 --> 00:33:24,825
23:08, JUNE 21, THURSDAY

524
00:33:28,265 --> 00:33:31,745
LOWER CARBON, GREENER LIVING

525
00:33:34,305 --> 00:33:36,345
If you really want
a piece of advice from me,

526
00:33:36,425 --> 00:33:37,865
it'll be to find a new job
as soon as possible.

527
00:33:39,105 --> 00:33:40,065
You're not fit for Lime.

528
00:33:43,785 --> 00:33:45,225
I'm staying, regardless.

529
00:33:53,985 --> 00:33:55,745
Hang on. Where are you heading?

530
00:33:55,825 --> 00:33:56,745
I have to hand over the shift soon.

531
00:33:56,825 --> 00:33:58,665
I can't give you a ride
if we're not going the same way.

532
00:33:58,745 --> 00:34:00,505
Tiantongyuan. Is that okay?

533
00:34:00,585 --> 00:34:02,505
It's too far. Sorry.
I don't have enough petrol.

534
00:34:15,865 --> 00:34:17,705
Want a ride? Where to?

535
00:34:17,784 --> 00:34:20,665
-I… I'm going to Tiantongyuan.
-One hundred and twenty yuan.

536
00:34:21,545 --> 00:34:22,505
That's too expensive.

537
00:34:22,585 --> 00:34:23,985
Expensive?

538
00:34:24,065 --> 00:34:25,145
Do you know what time it is?

539
00:34:25,225 --> 00:34:26,264
No one goes there anymore.

540
00:34:26,344 --> 00:34:27,625
Hop in. Let's go.

541
00:34:39,304 --> 00:34:40,385
Hop in.

542
00:34:43,905 --> 00:34:46,185
No, thanks. I found a cab.

543
00:34:46,264 --> 00:34:48,145
It's illegal to stop here.

544
00:35:03,465 --> 00:35:05,465
He's driving a Mercedes-Benz
and yet he's stealing my business.

545
00:35:08,185 --> 00:35:10,105
JING Z 59Q00

546
00:35:13,305 --> 00:35:14,545
Fasten your seat belt.

547
00:35:28,145 --> 00:35:29,185
Thanks, Luke.

548
00:35:30,625 --> 00:35:32,305
You may drop me off in front.

549
00:35:32,905 --> 00:35:34,145
I'll hail a cab back.

550
00:35:35,945 --> 00:35:38,065
Drop you off so that you can get
into another scam cab?

551
00:35:39,105 --> 00:35:42,025
There was a piece of chewing gum
on that scammer's license plate.

552
00:35:42,105 --> 00:35:42,945
The O on it became a Q.

553
00:35:49,865 --> 00:35:51,625
Stop looking at it. Where do you stay?

554
00:35:54,625 --> 00:35:55,625
Luke.

555
00:35:55,705 --> 00:35:57,905
I live quite far away.

556
00:35:58,505 --> 00:35:59,665
My home is in Tiantongyuan.

557
00:35:59,745 --> 00:36:00,825
I don't want to trouble you.

558
00:36:03,145 --> 00:36:04,145
You don't want to trouble me?

559
00:36:04,665 --> 00:36:06,985
You wrote in the interview
that I asked you to quit.

560
00:36:08,825 --> 00:36:11,585
HR said I couldn't make things up
for the interview,

561
00:36:11,665 --> 00:36:13,865
so I was being honest.

562
00:36:17,705 --> 00:36:19,305
You can be quite crafty.

563
00:36:19,825 --> 00:36:20,705
Just a bit, though.

564
00:36:38,065 --> 00:36:40,225
TIANTONG DONGYUAN

565
00:36:40,305 --> 00:36:42,385
-Is this the place?
-Yes, it's here.

566
00:36:42,465 --> 00:36:44,465
-Get out.
-Thanks.

567
00:36:52,025 --> 00:36:53,305
Luke.

568
00:36:53,825 --> 00:36:55,745
I am not challenging your authority.

569
00:36:55,825 --> 00:36:58,425
I have noted down
everything you said today.

570
00:37:01,905 --> 00:37:02,745
You noted it down?

571
00:37:04,225 --> 00:37:07,025
Are you using it against me immediately
and being a jerk

572
00:37:07,105 --> 00:37:08,585
or to get back at me?

573
00:37:11,025 --> 00:37:15,265
No. HR told me
to write everything down truthfully.

574
00:37:16,305 --> 00:37:18,065
Being only truthful
won't make you last in this industry.

575
00:37:18,985 --> 00:37:19,865
You're not fit for Lime.

576
00:37:19,945 --> 00:37:20,985
That's my real advice.

577
00:37:21,745 --> 00:37:22,665
Go home now.

578
00:37:26,825 --> 00:37:27,945
You…

579
00:37:28,465 --> 00:37:30,185
Why do you hate me so much?

580
00:37:31,305 --> 00:37:33,705
Is it because I ruined your typewriter?

581
00:37:33,785 --> 00:37:35,225
I can compensate you.

582
00:37:35,305 --> 00:37:37,385
Can I pay you back
through monthly installments?

583
00:37:38,065 --> 00:37:39,305
It has nothing to do with it.

584
00:37:39,825 --> 00:37:40,905
And you don't need to compensate me.

585
00:37:43,985 --> 00:37:45,185
I'm so sorry.

586
00:37:48,265 --> 00:37:49,265
I won't quit.

587
00:37:49,345 --> 00:37:50,785
Thank you for the lift.

588
00:37:59,225 --> 00:38:02,065
She looks meek,
as if anyone can bully her.

589
00:38:02,585 --> 00:38:04,625
But when she's mad, she will fight back.

590
00:38:05,625 --> 00:38:06,665
Just a little, that's all.

591
00:39:21,505 --> 00:39:23,545
Sun Yu. Sun Yu.

592
00:39:25,545 --> 00:39:26,425
Sun Yu!

593
00:39:56,185 --> 00:39:57,385
Help!

594
00:40:33,385 --> 00:40:34,785
LOWER CARBON, GREENER LIVING

595
00:40:42,145 --> 00:40:45,305
I am incredibly lucky and honored
to be able to work

596
00:40:45,385 --> 00:40:47,665
in this world-class advertising company.

597
00:40:47,745 --> 00:40:49,665
I will do my best to stay here.

598
00:41:01,145 --> 00:41:02,185
Hop in.

